---
import Pillar from '../../layouts/Pillar.astro';
import ChildGrid from '../../components/ChildGrid.astro';
import { CHILDREN } from '../../data/clusters';
import { SITE } from '../../consts';

const items = CHILDREN['home-golf'];
const schema = [{
  '@type': 'CollectionPage',
  name: 'Home Golf: Building a Practice Setup That Actually Gets Used',
  description: 'Golf simulators, launch monitors, nets, mats and enclosures — component by component, with realistic budgets and the costs nobody mentions upfront.',
  hasPart: items.map((i) => ({
    '@type': 'WebPage', name: i.title, url: new URL(i.href, SITE.url).href,
  })),
}];
---
<Pillar
  cluster="home-golf"
  title='Home Golf: Building a Practice Setup That Actually Gets Used'
  description='Golf simulators, launch monitors, nets, mats and enclosures — component by component, with realistic budgets and the costs nobody mentions upfront.'
  intro='A home setup is the difference between practising twice a month and practising four times a week. It is also the easiest place in golf to spend a great deal of money in the wrong order.'
  schema={schema}
>
  <div class="pil-prose">
      <h2>Build in the right order</h2>
      <p>
        The most common expensive mistake is buying the launch monitor first, then discovering the
        room cannot accommodate it. Space constrains everything, so measure before you shop.
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Measure the space.</strong> Ceiling height first — it decides whether you can swing a driver at all. Then width, then depth.</li>
        <li><strong>Choose the launch monitor.</strong> Camera-based units generally need space behind the ball; radar units generally need space in front. The room decides this, not the review scores.</li>
        <li><strong>Buy the best hitting mat you can afford.</strong> This is the component people under-spend on, and a hard mat punishes your wrists and elbows over time.</li>
        <li><strong>Then screen, enclosure, projector and software</strong>, in whatever order the budget allows.</li>
      </ol>

      <div class="callout callout-warn">
        <p class="callout-title">The costs that surprise people</p>
        <p>
          Budget for the things that never appear in a headline package price: a short-throw
          projector if the room is tight, a computer capable of running the software, lighting
          consistent enough for a camera-based unit, and flooring or side netting to protect the
          room. On a mid-range build these routinely add a third to the total.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Measured versus estimated data</h2>
      <p>
        This distinction matters more than any brand comparison. Every launch monitor
        <em>measures</em> some values and <em>calculates</em> the rest from a model. A unit that
        measures ball speed and estimates spin will look confident and be wrong in exactly the
        situations where you most need it to be right. Before comparing prices, find out which
        metrics each unit actually measures &mdash; our
        <a href="/home-golf/launch-monitors/">launch monitor guide</a> covers how to tell, for
        any unit, from its own spec sheet.
      </p>

      <div class="callout callout-key">
        <p class="callout-title">Measure the room before you shop</p>
        <p>
          The <a href="/tools/simulator-budget/">space and budget planner</a> checks whether your
          ceiling, depth and width can host a full swing and a launch monitor, then splits your
          budget across the components in the order above &mdash; including the costs that never
          appear in a package price. It publishes no prices, because we do not repeat figures we
          have not verified. The full structure is in the
          <a href="/home-golf/simulator-cost/">cost guide</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
  </div>

  <ChildGrid items={items} heading="Guides in this section" />
</Pillar>

<style>
  .pil-prose { max-width: var(--w-prose); }
  .pil-prose :global(h2) { margin-top: var(--s-7); font-size: var(--fs-xl); }
  .pil-prose :global(li) { margin-bottom: var(--s-2); }
  .pil-prose :global(li::marker) { color: var(--brand); }
  .pil-prose :global(.table-scroll) { max-width: var(--w-content); }
</style>
